diff --git a/docs/api/sections/authentication.md b/docs/api/sections/authentication.md
index f06ea6e..937790e 100644
--- a/docs/api/sections/authentication.md
+++ b/docs/api/sections/authentication.md
@@ -69,12 +69,16 @@ Set-Cookie: pending_authentication_token=...; HttpOnly; SameSite=Lax
 
 The response includes a `pending_authentication_token` both in the JSON body and as a cookie.
 Native apps should store this token and include it as a cookie when submitting the magic link code.
+The token, like the code, is good for 15 minutes.
+
+When sign ups are open, an unknown email address is signed up on the spot and gets a code too. Otherwise
+the response looks the same but no code is sent and the token is `null`, so email addresses can't be probed.
 
 __Error responses:__
 
 | Status Code | Description |
 |--------|-------------|
-| `422 Unprocessable entity` | Invalid email address, if sign ups are enabled and the value isn't a valid email address |
+| `422 Unprocessable entity` | The value isn't a valid email address |
 | `429 Too Many Requests` | Rate limit exceeded |
 
 ### 2. Submit the magic link code
